### [MEDIUM] `findPet` `@ModelAttribute` returns `null` — causes opaque NullPointerException — `GLD-STD-001@1 §4.1`
**File:** `PetController.java:76-87`

**Observed:** `Owner.getPet(Integer id)` (`Owner.java:117-127`) is documented to return `null` if
no pet with the given id belongs to the owner. `findPet` calls `owner.getPet(petId)` at line 86
and returns whatever it gets — potentially `null`. Any downstream handler that dereferences the
`@ModelAttribute("pet")` will throw a `NullPointerException` with no meaningful context.

**Risk (GLD-STD-001@1 §4.1):** The exception is not handled or re-raised with context; it is
swallowed by the framework and surfaces as a generic 500 — an unhandled case that violates §4.1.

**Fix:**

```java
// PetController.java:86
Pet pet = owner.getPet(petId);
if (pet == null) {
    throw new IllegalArgumentException("Pet not found: id=" + petId + " for ownerId=" + ownerId);
}
return pet;
```

The `@ControllerAdvice` recommended above will then render a clean 404.

