### [MEDIUM] Duplicate owner lookup in `findPet` — wasted DB round-trip and inconsistent error message
**File:** `PetController.java:83-85`

**Observed:** `findPet` looks up the `Owner` a *second* time (lines 83-85) even though `findOwner`
(lines 68-73) has already resolved the same `ownerId` for the same request. Spring will call both
`@ModelAttribute` methods, performing two identical repository reads.

**Risk:** Wasted DB call per request; two slightly different error messages for the same condition
("Please ensure the ID is correct " — note the trailing space — vs the message in `findOwner`),
making log analysis harder.

**Fix:** Inject the already-resolved `@ModelAttribute("owner")` Owner into `findPet` instead of
re-fetching:

```java
@ModelAttribute("pet")
public Pet findPet(@ModelAttribute("owner") Owner owner,
                   @PathVariable(name = "petId", required = false) Integer petId) {
    if (petId == null) {
        return new Pet();
    }
    Pet pet = owner.getPet(petId);
    if (pet == null) {
        throw new IllegalArgumentException("Pet not found: id=" + petId + " for ownerId=" + owner.getId());
    }
    return pet;
}
```

