- **`@InitBinder` correctly disallows `id` and `*.id`** on both controllers (`OwnerController.java:61`,
  `PetController.java:91`, `PetController.java:97`). This prevents mass-assignment of surrogate
  keys — a good defensive control.
- **Bean Validation is applied at the boundary** via `@Valid` on all mutating handler parameters,
  consistent with `GLD-STD-001@1 §3.1`.
- **Birth-date validation** in `PetController` correctly rejects future dates at the controller
  level before hitting the domain, which is the right layer per §3.1.
- **`DataIntegrityViolationException` is re-raised** (not silently swallowed) when it is not a
  known duplicate — the intent of `GLD-STD-001@1 §4.1` is respected for that branch, even though
  it still needs to be logged.
- **Owner ID mismatch check** in `OwnerController.processUpdateOwnerForm` (`line 149`) guards
  against URL/body ID tampering — a sound correctness control.

